=== BLOCKED_SUMMARY ===
Three independent blockers, none of which this prompt can fix
within its allowed-files list:

A. ANCHORED GREP (gate step #2) returns 153 violation lines across
   38 source files. 150 of the 153 are references to tables that the
   prompt drops AND that 000169-000175 immediately recreate with new
   SI columns -- in other words, false positives produced by a regex
   that cannot distinguish "dropped legacy" from "dropped + recreated".
   The remaining 3 hits (`fleet_telemetry_subscriptions` in
   `internal/database/fleet_subscription_repo.go`, called from
   `internal/api/devtools_handler.go`) are genuine; that table is
   truly dropped and not recreated, and no consumer-migration prompt
   covers the devtools/repo files where those references live.

B. CROSS-SERVICE GREP (gate step #3) is structurally unable to
   distinguish a SQL table name from a URL path segment ("/drives"),
   an English noun ("drives" in docs prose), an i18n label, a feature
   directory name (`web/src/features/drives/`), a React component
   (`DrivesPage`), or a TypeScript field. The previous BLOCKED log
   measured this at 1028 hits and concluded the check would need to
   be narrowed to be a credible correctness signal. (Not exercised
   in this run because step #2 fails first.)

C. APPLY-TEST PRE-EXISTENCE (gate step #7) hard-fails because
   `func TestMigrationApply` does not exist anywhere in the repo, and
   the 0078 allowed-files list excludes test files so the test cannot
   be authored within this prompt's scope.

